#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133554 :question/id #uuid "6e47a532-ba7a-5692-961b-eabc743d74e6" :question/math-academy-id "e-4734" :question/problem "Suppose we are applying these two elementary row operations, in the given order, to a $3\\times 3$ matrix $A\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\nR_2\\leftrightarrow R_3, \\qquad\n\tR_1:=6R_1\n$$\n\nFind the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication." :question/worked-solution "First, let's find the elementary matrices corresponding to the two given elementary row operations.\n\n- The first operation is $R_2\\leftrightarrow R_3.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={E}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The second operation is $R_1:=6R_1.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & :=6{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={E}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo apply the first elementary row operation to the matrix $A,$ we multiply by $E_1$ on the left and get $E_1 A\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n{\\left[ \\begin{array}{ccc}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0\\end{array} \\right]}\n\\cdot\nA\n$$\n\nThen, to apply the second elementary row operation to $E_1 A,$ we multiply by $E_2$ on the left and get $E_2 E_1 A\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n{\\left[ \\begin{array}{ccc}6 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{array} \\right]}\n\\cdot\n{\\left[ \\begin{array}{ccc}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0\\end{array} \\right]}\n\\cdot\nA\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134187 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "513943d2-1db7-5bd9-894d-91ed6db1e89b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "A\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297894} {:answer/id #uuid "59b146cf-7c47-5272-adde-0fe2b03d0023" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297927} {:answer/id #uuid "6aa36ea0-e3ae-5332-9259-bc9db485b5ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "A\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298011} {:answer/id #uuid "cde70c7f-2559-522c-bab1-89f8bf6027ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -3\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298451} {:answer/id #uuid "d844c09e-5c6d-5030-a943-16e6c8476759" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298480}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d844c09e-5c6d-5030-a943-16e6c8476759" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298480} :answer-field/id #uuid "ff80a385-216a-5db4-94f4-9a630195c374" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299496}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "5850f9b5-76bb-54cc-bfaa-176ac2b82ca9" :question/math-academy-id "q-32128" :question/problem "Suppose that the elementary row operation ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-3{R}_{3}$ is applied to a $3\\times 3$ matrix $A.$ What is the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication?" :question/worked-solution "We need to find a matrix $E$ such that $EA$ is equivalent to applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-3{R}_{3}$ to $A.$\n\nTo find $E,$ we apply the given row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-3{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =E\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication is $EA:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134188 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "13eaadff-3687-536c-9152-b822fc375060" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555037} {:answer/id #uuid "2a01eca5-fa0b-5049-a53c-e833416850dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555092} {:answer/id #uuid "95c99992-7a25-56fc-b648-98f6f4e070fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555356} {:answer/id #uuid "a71ff639-c19d-5070-b6d6-ad4beb6b2067" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555399} {:answer/id #uuid "b8f3a67a-ab60-54b5-8baa-d26326e591b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555440}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "13eaadff-3687-536c-9152-b822fc375060" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555037} :answer-field/id #uuid "66a11fe9-898d-5b2a-8aed-653455c9c121" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131167}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "82b71e56-3d28-5ee4-abda-f6f05cdef408" :question/math-academy-id "q-32134" :question/problem "Suppose that the following elementary row operations are applied to a $3\\times 3$ matrix $A$ in the given order:\n\n$$\n{R}_{1}↔{R}_{3},\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-2{R}_{3},\\,{R}_{1}:=3{R}_{1}\n$$\n\nWhat is the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication?" :question/worked-solution "First, let's find the elementary matrices corresponding to the given elementary row operations.\n\n- The first operation is ${R}_{1}↔{R}_{3}.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={E}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The second operation is ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-2{R}_{3}.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-2{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={E}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The third operation is ${R}_{1}:=3{R}_{1}.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & :=3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={E}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo apply the first elementary row operation to the matrix $A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{1}$ on the left and get ${E}_{1}A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A\n$$\n\nThen, to apply the second elementary row operation to ${E}_{1}A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{2}$ on the left and get ${E}_{2}{E}_{1}A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A\n$$\n\nFinally, to apply the third elementary row operation to ${E}_{2}{E}_{1}A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{3}$ on the left and get ${E}_{3}{E}_{2}{E}_{1}A:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134189 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "21948faf-e95a-5edb-90cb-1da55120bdf5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{2}:=-3{R}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477799} {:answer/id #uuid "40e9e6a6-42dc-5c43-8d3d-b1154d529448" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-\\frac{2}{3}{R}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477856} {:answer/id #uuid "47c8ae66-6c47-5457-9c0b-2626458218ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{2}:=-\\frac{2}{3}{R}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477875} {:answer/id #uuid "51569822-4746-5054-a95a-35b8d1b9b4f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-\\frac{3}{2}{R}_{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477901} {:answer/id #uuid "7ffad30d-316a-5348-befb-64ed01e69f4d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{2}:=-\\frac{3}{2}{R}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478001}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "47c8ae66-6c47-5457-9c0b-2626458218ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{2}:=-\\frac{2}{3}{R}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477875} :answer-field/id #uuid "49db34c5-1a78-58e6-9b61-a2209475d815" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131173}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "0972695d-55f6-56a5-a84e-e125e7bacf50" :question/math-academy-id "q-32145" :question/problem "Consider $E=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -\\frac{2}{3} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$ and a $3\\times 3$ matrix $A.$ Find the row operation that, when applied to $A,$ is equivalent to multiplying $A$ by the given elementary matrix $E$ from the left." :question/worked-solution "The given matrix $E$ is obtained by multiplying the second row of ${I}_{3}$ by $-\\frac{2}{3}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{3} & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :=-\\frac{2}{3}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -\\frac{2}{3} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =E\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $EA$ is equivalent to applying the elementary \nrow operation ${R}_{2}:=-\\frac{2}{3}{R}_{2}$ to $A.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134190 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0f052266-a78d-53f6-a624-dbcfb60c6b7a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}-{R}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300017} {:answer/id #uuid "28489d41-fcfe-5fbd-aa9f-58d8c03fdfa3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{1}↔{R}_{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300156} {:answer/id #uuid "447d16d4-e4ed-5411-a267-a5cd72c6a62a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{1}↔{R}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300301} {:answer/id #uuid "78150501-86d3-5ad2-b18d-3aa575407c19" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{2}:=2{R}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300553} {:answer/id #uuid "e840a680-6695-5b5e-b17d-1a0d7769e11b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+{R}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301110}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "447d16d4-e4ed-5411-a267-a5cd72c6a62a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{1}↔{R}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300301} :answer-field/id #uuid "e8eef8d5-a521-5905-9cae-619b2505ad27" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301965}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "67780f7b-b335-51d6-8512-e61d1ae7ee4f" :question/math-academy-id "q-32147" :question/problem "Consider $E=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$ and a $3\\times 3$ matrix $A.$\nFind the row operation that, when applied to $A,$ is equivalent to multiplying $A$ by the given elementary matrix $E$ from the left." :question/worked-solution "The given matrix $E$ is obtained by swapping the first and the second rows of ${I}_{3}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{3} & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =E\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $EA$ is equivalent to applying the elementary \nrow operation ${R}_{1}↔{R}_{2}$ to $A.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134393 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2d65d5f6-e3b7-5ee9-95cf-58c3e498a702" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459975} {:answer/id #uuid "646a048e-f630-5013-95fe-6659b566a35f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459976}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "646a048e-f630-5013-95fe-6659b566a35f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459976} :answer-field/id #uuid "34d3f262-127e-5585-b97c-20a126667044" :answer-field/key "$A$ has a zero column" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460854} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8460f2bb-e253-5210-9218-4e96e796beae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459977} {:answer/id #uuid "40f38a8d-b50e-505f-9411-5989253d0642" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459978}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8460f2bb-e253-5210-9218-4e96e796beae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459977} :answer-field/id #uuid "cde9df91-1435-51c4-9805-9c117768203b" :answer-field/key "$A$ has identical columns" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460855} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d90e2fb7-b1da-50a5-82da-f4e30f796fcc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459979} {:answer/id #uuid "8df48ba2-f889-595c-9590-a8404cf9b0b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459980}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8df48ba2-f889-595c-9590-a8404cf9b0b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459980} :answer-field/id #uuid "f677a744-3bd0-564b-ade4-affd6abcf2a2" :answer-field/key "$A$ has identical rows" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460856}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "2d571c31-8e0e-520c-b34f-482cf5518003" :question/math-academy-id "q-42458" :question/problem "$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix given above. Identify **all** of the reasons why one can conclude that $|A|=0?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the statements in turn.\n\n- $A$ has a zero column: \n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\\,✓\n$$\n\n- $A$ does *not* have identical columns.\n\n- $A$ has identical rows: \n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 4\\end{bmatrix}.\\,✓\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “$A$ has a zero column”; “$A$ has identical rows” only."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134394 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4731d43a-1037-5467-97a5-e798a96ef9d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327555} {:answer/id #uuid "658a8d30-d9af-5e26-83da-9719b1081d76" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327818} {:answer/id #uuid "6d1056e6-0216-54a8-a348-f7fd16cd261c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327879} {:answer/id #uuid "cb4f71df-9ae0-539d-bc37-b9dfa1a2efd4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328715} {:answer/id #uuid "f61627d1-d9a7-5fa0-8601-a797fc2e5d46" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329093}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f61627d1-d9a7-5fa0-8601-a797fc2e5d46" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329093} :answer-field/id #uuid "3ecac406-0aef-584c-9d48-0a6c47d439e8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329307}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "a804e446-7433-50c7-a8ce-2769d7a93237" :question/math-academy-id "q-42459" :question/problem "Find $4det(A)+4det(B)$, where \n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}2\\sqrt{2} & 1 \\\\ 1 & \\sqrt{2}\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & \\sqrt{2} & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 6 & 6\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each matrix in turn.\n\n- For the matrix $A,$ we have\n\n$$\ndet(A)=2\\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\sqrt{2}-1\\cdot 1=3.\n$$\n\n- Since $B$ has proportional columns, we obtain\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & \\sqrt{2} & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 6 & 6\\end{bmatrix}\\,⟹\\,det(B)=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $4det(A)+4det(B)=4\\cdot 3+4\\cdot 0=12.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134395 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c225eb90-e2e0-5316-bf2c-433fb3c69768" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132410} {:answer/id #uuid "320e4a8c-eedf-5588-98e8-c145e0ace715" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132411} {:answer/id #uuid "43de3423-2ffd-5930-9ee0-ea5001c9a16b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132412} {:answer/id #uuid "53f34a5f-dc76-5b22-9b1f-04217732f9e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132413} {:answer/id #uuid "796055cc-72c1-5b68-9805-3a39d9b06647" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132414}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c225eb90-e2e0-5316-bf2c-433fb3c69768" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132410} :answer-field/id #uuid "33879ed2-4ff8-5792-966a-daa49f7bc975" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132409}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "dcb38d39-eeab-5f94-bc9b-9cb1d6df2c04" :question/math-academy-id "q-42461" :question/problem "Find $2det(A)+4det(B)$, where \n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & \\sqrt{3} & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & \\sqrt{2} & 2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 0 & \\sqrt{2} \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each matrix in turn.\n\n- Since $A$ is a triangular matrix, its determinant is given by the product of the elements of the main diagonal: \n\n$$\ndet(A)=1\\cdot 2\\cdot 2\\cdot 1=4\n$$\n\n- Since $B$ has two identical rows, we obtain\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & \\sqrt{2} & 2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 0 & \\sqrt{2} \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\,⟹\\,det(B)=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $2det(A)+4det(B)=2\\cdot 4+4\\cdot 0=8.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134396 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ae722046-6be9-5e9a-bf56-4206a9c79894" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -\\frac{1}{3} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132416} {:answer/id #uuid "10dc647e-4bc7-5382-9e97-bd8139145536" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "A \\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -\\frac{1}{3} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132417} {:answer/id #uuid "24d766ed-85a6-59fa-8b22-a6ac0c017b06" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "A \\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{3} & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132418} {:answer/id #uuid "27406f2d-9f97-5baa-af72-688260907814" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -\\frac{1}{3} & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132419} {:answer/id #uuid "591aa2fa-7ddf-5186-a24b-309823941754" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{3}\\end{bmatrix} \\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132420}] :answer-field/id #uuid "0b77ad91-bb09-5ec1-ad51-91b9ef6f7291" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132415}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "f3396ef1-1f68-5e2b-b91b-41c595c5178e" :question/math-academy-id "q-42532" :question/problem "Suppose that the elementary row operation\n$R_{2}:=-\\frac{1}{3}R_{2}$ is applied to a $3 \\cdot 3$ matrix $A$. What is the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication?"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134397 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0f5382a8-b164-5842-8bcb-3b9d053952ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555028} {:answer/id #uuid "22deabc5-9aad-5613-943c-caa43316c3b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555069} {:answer/id #uuid "7e1d6c63-aad1-5e3b-a248-e384ccce98f7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555289} {:answer/id #uuid "92c2751f-4193-5c6f-97dd-244f23ad8709" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555344} {:answer/id #uuid "d95d2362-22f9-57be-9151-562448a59ab9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555525}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0f5382a8-b164-5842-8bcb-3b9d053952ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555028} :answer-field/id #uuid "1017a124-cd54-55e1-978b-fc33a296608e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132421}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "b1dbb1aa-689b-52a9-913e-1f549be5077b" :question/math-academy-id "q-42538" :question/problem "Suppose that the following elementary row operations are applied to a $3\\times 3$ matrix $A$ in the given order:\n\n$$\n{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+2{R}_{3},\\,{R}_{2}:=-3{R}_{2}\n$$\n\nWhat is the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication?" :question/worked-solution "First, let's find the elementary matrices corresponding to the given elementary row operations.\n\n- The first operation is ${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+2{R}_{3}.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+2{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={E}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The second operation is ${R}_{2}:=-3{R}_{2}.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :=-3{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={E}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo apply the first elementary row operation to the matrix $A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{1}$ on the left and get ${E}_{1}A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A\n$$\n\nThen, to apply the second elementary row operation to ${E}_{1}A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{2}$ on the left and get ${E}_{2}{E}_{1}A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot A\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134407 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ba7d7bc9-77ef-583c-8caa-22315aad7aca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$|A|$, $|B|$, and $|C|$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392523} {:answer/id #uuid "23f02ed7-eb83-5988-a1ca-ee80eac659ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$|B|$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392524} {:answer/id #uuid "d767aec8-a44c-5175-bbcd-b71f577015fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$|A|$ and $|C|$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392525} {:answer/id #uuid "ee7ae539-44fc-5d03-b8b9-5a5b498db62e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$|A|$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392526} {:answer/id #uuid "3737a2a5-a57d-571a-a651-f2cad4ee3049" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$|A|$ and $|B|$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392527}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d767aec8-a44c-5175-bbcd-b71f577015fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$|A|$ and $|C|$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392525} :answer-field/id #uuid "00ef10bc-f305-5726-8271-949923025e38" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392522}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "cee2c526-7176-535a-81f7-173bfaefecec" :question/math-academy-id "q-42882" :question/problem "Which of the following determinants are equal to $0?$\n\n$$\n|A|=\\begin{vmatrix}2 & -1 & \\sqrt{3} \\\\ \\sqrt[5]{2} & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{vmatrix},\\,|B|=\\begin{vmatrix}1 & \\sqrt{2} & 4 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4\\end{vmatrix},\\,|C|=\\begin{vmatrix}1 & \\sqrt{2} & 4 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 8 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 4\\end{vmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the given determinants in turn.\n\n- The matrix $A$ has a zero row: \n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 & \\sqrt{3} \\\\ \\sqrt[5]{2} & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nAs a result, $|A|=0.$\n\n- The matrix $B$ is a triangular matrix, hence \n\n$$\n|B|=1\\cdot 3\\cdot 4=12\\ne 0.\n$$\n\n- The matrix $C$ has proportional columns: \n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & \\sqrt{2} & 4 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 8 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nAs a result, $|C|=0.$\n\nTherefore, only $|A|$ and $|C|$ are equal to $0.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134408 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "025d4fe7-912b-5dd2-9e59-0f9e27e42564" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$|A|$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326959} {:answer/id #uuid "0b78b8cf-6e3b-5e97-89b9-e4607f53b9c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$|A|$ and $|B|$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327035} {:answer/id #uuid "68941b7c-87c5-5d4d-a0c5-f9192e02ec8b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$|B|$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327836} {:answer/id #uuid "9231df0a-ccd7-5f2a-9501-f2efeb7f0ccf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$|A|$, $|B|$, and $|C|$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328205} {:answer/id #uuid "dcc18135-f248-5156-83fe-02e74da6694d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$|A|$ and $|C|$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328862}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dcc18135-f248-5156-83fe-02e74da6694d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$|A|$ and $|C|$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328862} :answer-field/id #uuid "a1401c3e-df25-5867-8647-15f11560a136" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329457}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "bf123fc4-eb0a-5072-9e49-491e1d68008c" :question/math-academy-id "q-42959" :question/problem "Which of the following determinants are equal to $0?$\n\n$$\n|A|=\\begin{vmatrix}2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ \\sqrt{5} & 0 & 4 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 0\\end{vmatrix},\\,|B|=\\begin{vmatrix}3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5\\end{vmatrix},\\,|C|=\\begin{vmatrix}4 & \\sqrt{3} & 4 \\\\ 2 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 1 & \\sqrt{5} & 1\\end{vmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the given determinants in turn.\n\n- The matrix $A$ has a zero column: \n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ \\sqrt{5} & 0 & 4 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nAs a result, $|A|=0.$\n\n- Since $B$ is a diagonal matrix, we obtain \n\n$$\n|B|=3\\cdot (-1)\\cdot 5=-15\\ne 0.\n$$\n\n- The matrix $C$ has identical columns: \n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & \\sqrt{3} & 4 \\\\ 2 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 1 & \\sqrt{5} & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nAs a result, $|C|=0.$\n\nTherefore, only $|A|$ and $|C|$ are equal to $0.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134414 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8cc3eb36-fa25-5b0c-a9f4-d0d9b6fd431c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448644} {:answer/id #uuid "024de02f-c585-5ff1-ae1f-906a7964b6c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448645}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8cc3eb36-fa25-5b0c-a9f4-d0d9b6fd431c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448644} :answer-field/id #uuid "f4ba6b54-8b9e-5c38-a842-718279128c22" :answer-field/key "$A$ has two identical rows" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449362} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a8759331-0ea5-5e82-a056-c79e5438af33" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448646} {:answer/id #uuid "e2f5cff8-7a78-538b-955f-a82c9351731b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448647}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e2f5cff8-7a78-538b-955f-a82c9351731b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448647} :answer-field/id #uuid "ae83d106-f07c-5d04-9fd2-5832bd202f49" :answer-field/key "One of the rows/columns of $A$ is proportional to another row/column of $A$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449363} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "318ceaba-c9a3-5098-81fd-4d438f7912e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448648} {:answer/id #uuid "773df97a-4a06-5ac8-b5d2-9731cc8bba08" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448649}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "318ceaba-c9a3-5098-81fd-4d438f7912e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448648} :answer-field/id #uuid "93e5158f-ae92-576e-abfb-6ad450c72c06" :answer-field/key "$A$ has two identical columns" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449364}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "ef67ff18-5c70-5c00-bdf0-27b79dc90b72" :question/math-academy-id "q-43306" :question/problem "Let $A$ be a $2\\times 2$ matrix such that $|A|=0.$ Which of the following statements must be true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's consider our statements in turn.\n\n- Statements “$A$ has two identical rows” and “$A$ has two identical columns” are false. For example, consider the matrix \n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 8\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWe have that \n\n$$\n|A|=1\\cdot 8-4\\cdot 2=0\n$$\n\nbut $A$ has neither two identical rows nor two identical columns.\n\n- Statement “One of the rows/columns of $A$ is proportional to another row/column of $A$” is true. Indeed, we can make use of the following fact:\n\n$|A|=0$ *if and only if one of the rows/columns of $A$ is a linear combination of other rows/columns of $A.$*\n\nIn the case of a $2\\times 2$ matrix, this means that one of the rows/columns must be proportional to another row/column.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “One of the rows/columns of $A$ is proportional to another row/column of $A$” only."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186240984 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1ae96c9c-5077-5b4e-bce5-938adb6a5bc0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238280} {:answer/id #uuid "33c2cd95-5c08-5d5a-9e16-58443a45fdf4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238503} {:answer/id #uuid "3d876cfd-c9a8-56e1-ae3b-34704eccf96b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238591} {:answer/id #uuid "88b9849d-4e76-5a49-87a7-7174e3308593" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239243} {:answer/id #uuid "8d4e7316-49d2-54a2-8310-bd6fdca5c7cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239282}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1ae96c9c-5077-5b4e-bce5-938adb6a5bc0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238280} :answer-field/id #uuid "3d2aa0b0-6bd4-510a-8baa-0533d84db54e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240437}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "b99af0d8-b75f-54bf-9697-c5d904e35653" :question/math-academy-id "q-105152" :question/problem "Find $h$, if $3{a}_{1}+h{a}_{2}=b$ and\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 14 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the properties of addition/subtraction and scalar multiplication of vectors to isolate the $h$ term, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{a}_{1}+h{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ 3\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}+h\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 14 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ h\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 14 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}-3\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ h\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-6 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 8 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the final equation above, we can tell that $h=2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186240985 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3e50e51d-23eb-52c3-9024-a155dbcb84d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238599} {:answer/id #uuid "47f8e849-3b9d-567e-a60c-02d76b96bff7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238681} {:answer/id #uuid "65cf35a9-f5a8-57f6-9ae1-12945a1cfe78" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238945} {:answer/id #uuid "f32999ff-ea41-5018-8e37-5fc7900e986b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240199} {:answer/id #uuid "fcf14835-4d02-58b4-9f69-fea39453dad5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240289}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "47f8e849-3b9d-567e-a60c-02d76b96bff7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238681} :answer-field/id #uuid "5deddcca-b475-5a82-9e89-09dc2f28ecf3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240503}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "ab1a2dbb-2f20-5b38-9d5d-1509f7f1ce65" :question/math-academy-id "q-105154" :question/problem "Find $m$, if $7{a}_{1}+m{a}_{2}=b$ and\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -12\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the properties of addition/subtraction and scalar multiplication of vectors to isolate the $m$ term, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7{a}_{1}+m{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ 7\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}+m\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -12\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ m\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -12\\end{bmatrix}-7\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ m\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-15 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the final equation above, we can tell that $m=-5.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186240986 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "55242c77-3e41-5fa2-b4bb-748f8cda0851" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238791} {:answer/id #uuid "5c71a2b1-85ca-5099-8f54-6e98685b9f3b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238863} {:answer/id #uuid "b3e09a56-8be6-5f0b-a232-4fefca913f23" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239626} {:answer/id #uuid "ee094296-26d3-56b8-8c76-a17091ddddcf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240152} {:answer/id #uuid "fd7a4f06-5e87-52ca-9c4b-04bdd6d58484" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240298}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5c71a2b1-85ca-5099-8f54-6e98685b9f3b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238863} :answer-field/id #uuid "a319c274-8067-5830-8026-4fd1f3678588" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240619}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "0970eb33-9f16-5468-a48a-ce3c4e9ea202" :question/math-academy-id "q-105159" :question/problem "Find $x$, if $4a+3x=b$ and\n\n$$\na=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the properties of addition/subtraction and scalar multiplication of vectors to isolate $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4a+3x & =b \\\\ 3x & =b-4a \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{3}(b-4a) \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{3}(\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}-4\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}) \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{3}\\begin{bmatrix}-9 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 15\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ x & =\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186240987 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "078a9ec2-ec45-5cb3-9fa6-fafc704f3a74" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238137} {:answer/id #uuid "0fc0872c-5cbc-50aa-a104-55f19e6b295e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238190} {:answer/id #uuid "3859506a-2f62-51f2-9746-b6b6e6ad359c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238543} {:answer/id #uuid "7b700677-9bf6-5789-9d49-4fae8f9135eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239119} {:answer/id #uuid "a7a5b1bf-85fc-59df-966b-dfb82ea3d6cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239508}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7b700677-9bf6-5789-9d49-4fae8f9135eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239119} :answer-field/id #uuid "e10a3090-0273-566f-800d-479ce03b72bf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240725}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "308d5a63-8dfe-5681-a74a-191ce78c4eb4" :question/math-academy-id "q-105160" :question/problem "Find the value of ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}$ given that $3a-5x=b$ and\n\n$$\na=\\begin{bmatrix}-6 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix},\\,x=\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}-13 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the properties of addition/subtraction and scalar multiplication of vectors to isolate $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3a-5x & =b \\\\ -5x & =b-3a \\\\ x & =-\\frac{1}{5}(b-3a) \\\\ x & =-\\frac{1}{5}(\\begin{bmatrix}-13 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}-3\\begin{bmatrix}-6 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}) \\\\ x & =-\\frac{1}{5}\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -10 \\\\ -15\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ x & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=-1+2=1.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186240988 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "477c777c-4fcf-504a-b88b-0251c8d7a259" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238678} {:answer/id #uuid "6e63b088-eae4-5df4-a692-469894ca6ec1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239006} {:answer/id #uuid "7f9b6079-8d41-5d56-a4ff-12d7e702dec9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239167} {:answer/id #uuid "b78c0e7b-505a-54ad-9372-3b394b39ce62" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239654} {:answer/id #uuid "e676cf21-c546-5aee-9ff8-268bb691b292" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240080}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7f9b6079-8d41-5d56-a4ff-12d7e702dec9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239167} :answer-field/id #uuid "31ef6744-d09a-5274-adfa-0de0cc8cac5c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240421}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "665aac1d-ba76-55e8-8058-f38999b08deb" :question/math-academy-id "q-105161" :question/problem "Find the value of ${x}_{1}-{x}_{2}$ given that $7a+4x=b$ and\n\n$$\na=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix},\\,x=\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{4}\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -6\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the properties of addition/subtraction and scalar multiplication of vectors to isolate $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7a+4x & =b \\\\ 4x & =b-7a \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{4}(b-7a) \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{4}(\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -6\\end{bmatrix}-7\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}) \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{4}\\begin{bmatrix}-8 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -20\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ x & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${x}_{1}-{x}_{2}=-2-1=-3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186240990 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "222862ae-7c2b-5d66-9d9a-f59640c9801e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238354} {:answer/id #uuid "346bdb71-8966-5ed4-ab2e-83d1ea69e239" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238507} {:answer/id #uuid "4072326e-9528-5390-aaaa-546988c57563" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238613} {:answer/id #uuid "4f101a20-f607-5e7e-b164-71aebdad2935" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238733} {:answer/id #uuid "61153d6d-bad7-5e46-a284-cae191fc9a25" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238908}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "346bdb71-8966-5ed4-ab2e-83d1ea69e239" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238507} :answer-field/id #uuid "47a0ee5a-75fc-5e2b-8002-cf62c42bfe1d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240456}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "a4963b43-3177-544a-ab68-1ea699a13395" :question/math-academy-id "q-105166" :question/problem "Consider the vectors\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nIf ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}=b,$ then what is ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "If ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}=b$, then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ -2{x}_{1} \\\\ 3{x}_{1}\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}2{x}_{2} \\\\ -3{x}_{2} \\\\ 5{x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2} \\\\ -2{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2} \\\\ 3{x}_{1}+5{x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nEquating the corresponding components, we get the following system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2} &=-3 \\\\ -2{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2} &=1 \\\\ 3{x}_{1}+5{x}_{2} &=-4\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nMultiplying the first equation by $2$ and adding the resulting equations, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & =-5,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich we substitute into the second equation to get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2}=1 \\\\ -2{x}_{1}-3(-5) & =1 \\\\ -2{x}_{1} & =-14 \\\\ {x}_{1} & =7.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute ${x}_{1}=7$ and ${x}_{2}=-5$ into the third equation and obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{x}_{1}+5{x}_{2}=-4 \\\\ 3(7)+5(-5) & =-4 \\\\ -4 & =-4,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives a true statement. \n\nSo the solution of the system is ${x}_{1}=7$ and ${x}_{2}=-5,$ which means\n\n$$\n7{a}_{1}-5{a}_{2}=b.\n$$\n\nConsequently, \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=7+(-5)=2.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186240991 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "05c3a1ce-60e5-59ff-a50a-13acd330b03f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238128} {:answer/id #uuid "16ccfa6d-4cbd-58be-a3d1-40e500abddf3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238250} {:answer/id #uuid "489d3697-4f9a-5294-985c-5ec2c27fe312" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238688} {:answer/id #uuid "51497961-e6a7-5e4d-9d38-e1cc46624ffe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238757} {:answer/id #uuid "bb3b3d4a-ea4e-52ba-aaca-a3a81abdfca7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239685}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bb3b3d4a-ea4e-52ba-aaca-a3a81abdfca7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239685} :answer-field/id #uuid "418087c6-543a-58e8-a946-98e11e2f5b50" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240444}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "d5149dd7-ead1-5d7c-a754-e514e2e6e606" :question/math-academy-id "q-105167" :question/problem "Consider the vectors\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}-7 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}-9 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nIf ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}=b,$ then what is ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "If ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}=b$, then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}-7 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-9 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}3{x}_{1} \\\\ -3{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{1}\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}-7{x}_{2} \\\\ 5{x}_{2} \\\\ -{x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-9 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}3{x}_{1}-7{x}_{2} \\\\ -3{x}_{1}+5{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{1}-{x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-9 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nEquating the corresponding components, we get the following system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}3{x}_{1}-7{x}_{2} &=-9 \\\\ -3{x}_{1}+5{x}_{2} &=3 \\\\ {x}_{1}-{x}_{2} &=1\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nAdding the first and the second equations we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2{x}_{2} & =-6 \\\\ {x}_{2} & =3,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich we substitute into the second equation to get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3{x}_{1}+5{x}_{2}=3 \\\\ -3{x}_{1}+5(3) & =3 \\\\ -3{x}_{1} & =-12 \\\\ {x}_{1} & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute ${x}_{1}=4$ and ${x}_{2}=3$ into the third equation and obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}=1 \\\\ (4)-(3) & =1 \\\\ 1 & =1,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives a true statement. \n\nSo the solution of the system is ${x}_{1}=4$ and ${x}_{2}=3,$ which means\n\n$$\n4{a}_{1}+3{a}_{2}=b.\n$$\n\nConsequently, \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=4+3=7.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186240992 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "24228b89-72c1-53f9-96a3-762f6e876413" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238375} {:answer/id #uuid "41f9a912-3fc6-5aa1-be4b-82da70d8f8d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238629} {:answer/id #uuid "48788366-6d42-5df1-818a-252fcb9e825d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238685} {:answer/id #uuid "67eb2257-68d5-593f-891b-6945f576e00f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238957} {:answer/id #uuid "d9f9576f-46f8-5778-888b-cb310e6c107d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239958}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "24228b89-72c1-53f9-96a3-762f6e876413" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238375} :answer-field/id #uuid "69b9e7b4-1521-54c5-b7f4-d54ad2ab9039" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240526}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "0d52be40-210e-5024-9a79-b6ca4323223c" :question/math-academy-id "q-105168" :question/problem "Consider the vectors\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ -8 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{3}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nIf ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=b,$ then what is ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}?$" :question/worked-solution "If ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=b$, then we have  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ -8 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{3}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ 3{x}_{1} \\\\ -2{x}_{1}\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}-3{x}_{2} \\\\ -8{x}_{2} \\\\ 6{x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}2{x}_{3} \\\\ 5{x}_{3} \\\\ -3{x}_{3}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2}+2{x}_{3} \\\\ 3{x}_{1}-8{x}_{2}+5{x}_{3} \\\\ -2{x}_{1}+6{x}_{2}-3{x}_{3}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding components, we get the following system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2}+2{x}_{3} &=2 \\\\ 3{x}_{1}-8{x}_{2}+5{x}_{3} &=1 \\\\ -2{x}_{1}+6{x}_{2}-3{x}_{3} &=2\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe will solve this system using Gaussian elimination. First, we write the augmented matrix for this system:\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -3 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 3 & -8 & 5 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 6 & -3 & 2\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the augmented matrix, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -3 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 3 & -8 & 5 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 6 & -3 & 2\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -3 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & -5 \\\\ -2 & 6 & -3 & 2\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -3 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 6\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2}+2{x}_{3} &=2 \\\\ {x}_{2}-{x}_{3} &=-5 \\\\ {x}_{3} &=6.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get ${x}_{3}=6.$ Substituting ${x}_{3}=6$ into the second equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}-6=-5\\,⟹\\,{x}_{2}=1.\n$$\n\nNow, substituting ${x}_{2}=1$ and ${x}_{3}=6$ into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}-3(1)+2(6)=2\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=-7.\n$$\n\nSo, the solution of the system is ${x}_{1}=-7$, ${x}_{2}=1$, and ${x}_{3}=6,$ which means \n\n$$\n-7{a}_{1}+{a}_{2}+6{a}_{3}=b.\n$$\n\nConsequently, \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=-7+1+6=0.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186240993 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "023fcb6e-19a9-5e78-8982-04f818ca611a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238099} {:answer/id #uuid "04fb8f1e-74de-53e7-811e-89afaef85a39" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238122} {:answer/id #uuid "60fcd9a2-4983-563f-a7a0-4d01c2393643" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238907} {:answer/id #uuid "b211c6b0-fbe0-52d2-9297-1454f53b6452" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "21" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239610} {:answer/id #uuid "f512eece-de08-5c13-ae53-369aa60ff55b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240219}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "023fcb6e-19a9-5e78-8982-04f818ca611a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238099} :answer-field/id #uuid "257c3c3e-fb71-526d-8119-cd61bd75c90e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240396}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "2b7aaa73-fdec-536a-866a-953c6856f39f" :question/math-academy-id "q-105169" :question/problem "Consider the vectors\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{3}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -8 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nIf ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=b,$ then what is ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}?$" :question/worked-solution "If ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=b$, then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{3}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -8 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ 5{x}_{1} \\\\ -2{x}_{1}\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{2} \\\\ 6{x}_{2} \\\\ -2{x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}-{x}_{3} \\\\ -8{x}_{3} \\\\ 2{x}_{3}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}-{x}_{3} \\\\ 5{x}_{1}+6{x}_{2}-8{x}_{3} \\\\ -2{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}+2{x}_{3}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding components, we get the following system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}-{x}_{3} &=2 \\\\ 5{x}_{1}+6{x}_{2}-8{x}_{3} &=-3 \\\\ -2{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}+2{x}_{3} &=4\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe will solve this system using Gaussian elimination. First, we write the augmented matrix for this system:\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 5 & 6 & -8 & -3 \\\\ -2 & -2 & 2 & 4\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the augmented matrix, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 5 & 6 & -8 & -3 \\\\ -2 & -2 & 2 & 4\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-5){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & -13 \\\\ -2 & -2 & 2 & 4\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & -13 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 8\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}-{x}_{3} &=2 \\\\ {x}_{2}-3{x}_{3} &=-13 \\\\ 0 &=8.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nHowever, the final equation $0=8$  gives a false statement. So the system has no solution."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186240994 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "200cb18f-f334-5cc1-92fe-59276f6e627e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238331} {:answer/id #uuid "355fb48b-9360-5e64-a49e-28f3e7ce5c33" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238517} {:answer/id #uuid "43ccb6b1-1509-50bb-81b1-0c4a73a41e16" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238644} {:answer/id #uuid "5d4f778a-7cda-5396-b040-7a95240b101b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238869} {:answer/id #uuid "ac46ea11-5d88-5152-b8a7-428c01fce429" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239552}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "43ccb6b1-1509-50bb-81b1-0c4a73a41e16" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238644} :answer-field/id #uuid "8483c7ae-14b3-59f6-a280-e2621e06ed0e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240565}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "e2bdebea-6388-5baf-ba9f-1fbe0535b5cc" :question/math-academy-id "q-105170" :question/problem "Consider the vectors\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 8\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{3}=\\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ -7 \\\\ 14\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nIf ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=b,$ then what is ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}?$" :question/worked-solution "If ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=b$, then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 8\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{3}\\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ -7 \\\\ 14\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ -{x}_{1} \\\\ 2{x}_{1}\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}4{x}_{2} \\\\ -3{x}_{2} \\\\ 8{x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}7{x}_{3} \\\\ -7{x}_{3} \\\\ 14{x}_{3}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1}+4{x}_{2}+7{x}_{3} \\\\ -{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2}-7{x}_{3} \\\\ 2{x}_{1}+8{x}_{2}+14{x}_{3}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding components, we get the following system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+4{x}_{2}+7{x}_{3} &=5 \\\\ -{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2}-7{x}_{3} &=-3 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}+8{x}_{2}+14{x}_{3} &=7\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe will solve this system using Gaussian elimination. First, we write the augmented matrix for this system:\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 4 & 7 & 5 \\\\ -1 & -3 & -7 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 8 & 14 & 7\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the augmented matrix, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 4 & 7 & 5 \\\\ -1 & -3 & -7 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 8 & 14 & 7\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 4 & 7 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 8 & 14 & 7\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 4 & 7 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -3\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+4{x}_{2}+7{x}_{3} &=5 \\\\ {x}_{2} &=2 \\\\ 0 &=-3.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nHowever, the final equation $0=-3$  gives a false statement. So the system has no solution."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186240995 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "43158102-a49d-59d4-a923-5df48591288f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238639} {:answer/id #uuid "7f08fc6f-64b7-5004-936e-7a6c7b50f76f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "17" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239160} {:answer/id #uuid "c032bb3d-2af4-5439-b0a3-83a63b9db908" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "19" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239727} {:answer/id #uuid "c25ef7e8-5b9c-591c-b034-15f9595ed22c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239760} {:answer/id #uuid "c7d1ebe2-d9a0-588f-835e-881ce34c1378" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239813}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "43158102-a49d-59d4-a923-5df48591288f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238639} :answer-field/id #uuid "83fca8c2-1efe-5ca1-813a-6af2b882ac08" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240564}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "e25147c5-4650-58c3-bac2-7139801cca6b" :question/math-academy-id "q-105172" :question/problem "Consider the vectors\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -5 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -21 \\\\ -12\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{3}=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 14 \\\\ 9\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 8 \\\\ -7\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nIf ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=b,$ then what is ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}?$" :question/worked-solution "If ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=b$, then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -5 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -21 \\\\ -12\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{3}\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 14 \\\\ 9\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 8 \\\\ -7\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ -5{x}_{1} \\\\ -3{x}_{1}\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}4{x}_{2} \\\\ -21{x}_{2} \\\\ -12{x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}-3{x}_{3} \\\\ 14{x}_{3} \\\\ 9{x}_{3}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 8 \\\\ -7\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1}+4{x}_{2}-3{x}_{3} \\\\ -5{x}_{1}-21{x}_{2}+14{x}_{3} \\\\ -3{x}_{1}-12{x}_{2}+9{x}_{3}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 8 \\\\ -7\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding components, we get the following system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+4{x}_{2}-3{x}_{3} &=2 \\\\ -5{x}_{1}-21{x}_{2}+14{x}_{3} &=8 \\\\ -3{x}_{1}-12{x}_{2}+9{x}_{3} &=-7\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe will solve this system using Gaussian elimination. First, we write the augmented matrix for this system:\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 4 & -3 & 2 \\\\ -5 & -21 & 14 & 8 \\\\ -3 & -12 & 9 & -7\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the augmented matrix, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 4 & -3 & 2 \\\\ -5 & -21 & 14 & 8 \\\\ -3 & -12 & 9 & -7\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+5{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 4 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -1 & 18 \\\\ -3 & -12 & 9 & -7\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 4 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -1 & 18 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -1\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+4{x}_{2}-3{x}_{3} &=2 \\\\ -{x}_{2}-{x}_{3} &=18 \\\\ 0 &=-1.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nHowever, the final equation $0=-1$  gives a false statement. So the system has no solution."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186241026 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "07a90ddc-0259-585f-9ae4-5617d9867886" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-6 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238138} {:answer/id #uuid "0db0933f-2b18-50f8-b5dd-6e96fe942217" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238174} {:answer/id #uuid "650d4b10-6c78-5b66-b132-1ec8fff7e67b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238938} {:answer/id #uuid "7ef45d2d-b0a6-5ab6-8951-91ce778b4f29" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239159} {:answer/id #uuid "c93b0e47-a83c-526d-8bd4-d6e268f20920" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239822}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c93b0e47-a83c-526d-8bd4-d6e268f20920" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239822} :answer-field/id #uuid "f14146b4-26f2-5e89-a173-b8e10576985c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240753}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "9add2d2a-fce4-5ca8-9b10-b0aa51d393b0" :question/math-academy-id "q-105294" :question/problem "The set ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ is linearly dependent. Which of the following vectors could be ${a}_{2}$ if\n$$\n\\displaystyle {a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}?\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We say that two vectors ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}$ are *linearly independent* if the only solution to the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}=0\n$$\n\nis ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=0.$ Otherwise, the vectors are *linearly dependent*.\n\nA set containing *only two* vectors is linearly *dependent* if and only if the two vectors are parallel.\n\nFrom the given options, the correct answer is\n\n$$\n{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -6\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTo see why, notice that \n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -6\\end{bmatrix}=(-2)\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}=-2{a}_{1}.\n$$\n\nThis way, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{a}_{1}-2{a}_{1} & =0 \\\\ 2{a}_{1}+{a}_{2} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn other words, the vectors ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{2}$ are parallel.\n\nTo see why this means that ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{2}$ are linearly dependent, we notice that the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}=0\n$$\n\nhas the solution ${x}_{1}=2$ and ${x}_{2}=1,$ which is different from ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=0.$ Therefore, the set is linearly dependent."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186241027 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "11a7491d-2ce9-57b5-afc5-475cffb86e52" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238202} {:answer/id #uuid "81792f0f-eb2e-5c8b-9e65-a32b2c8a647e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239178} {:answer/id #uuid "84b00443-b844-5946-b246-e24069d4f374" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239208} {:answer/id #uuid "c37a4610-6917-5cd7-8438-a4eaaee5a60f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239781} {:answer/id #uuid "d87befb5-db05-5e3b-b1bc-bbf4875296fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239945}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d87befb5-db05-5e3b-b1bc-bbf4875296fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239945} :answer-field/id #uuid "daefdae9-19ab-5066-96c6-64e5270f1794" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240715}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "6e5fd550-1965-59ea-b83f-2c578a1e0197" :question/math-academy-id "q-105296" :question/problem "The set $\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\}$ is linearly dependent. Which of the following vectors could be ${a}_{2}$ if\n$$\n\\displaystyle {a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}?\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We say that two vectors ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}$ are *linearly independent* if the only solution to the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}=0\n$$\n\nis ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=0.$ Otherwise, the vectors are *linearly dependent*.\n\nA set containing *only two* vectors is linearly *dependent* if and only if the two vectors are parallel.\n\nFrom the given options, the correct answer is \n\n$$\n{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n \n\nTo see why, notice that \n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}=-\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}=-\\frac{1}{2}{a}_{1}.\n$$\n\nThis way, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}{a}_{1}-\\frac{1}{2}{a}_{1} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}{a}_{1}+{a}_{2} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn other words, the vectors ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{2}$ are parallel.\n\nTo see why this means that ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{2}$ are linearly dependent, we notice that the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}=0\n$$\n\nhas the solution ${x}_{1}=\\frac{1}{2}$ and ${x}_{2}=1,$ which is different from ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=0.$ Therefore, the set is linearly dependent."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186241028 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1564190f-a603-5a1b-99ee-d29458e3bdf9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-10 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238231} {:answer/id #uuid "67430bf0-add9-5760-a0d2-5687fc3ea820" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ -10 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238953} {:answer/id #uuid "771afedc-1ab9-538b-9c8d-99514ab7bd87" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -10\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239082} {:answer/id #uuid "a297bb83-555e-542b-b729-eb9040d9fd2e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}10 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239468} {:answer/id #uuid "edc71038-d293-56dc-bedb-b4c724d2c367" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-10 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240151}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "edc71038-d293-56dc-bedb-b4c724d2c367" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-10 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240151} :answer-field/id #uuid "4b1c4cc2-96e9-5425-b903-8dcaac1d1c80" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240460}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "070a6728-701f-5a05-b9c9-03b5e1530505" :question/math-academy-id "q-105297" :question/problem "The set $\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\}$ is linearly dependent. Which of the following vectors could be ${a}_{2}$ if\n$$\n\\displaystyle {a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}?\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We say that two vectors ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}$ are *linearly independent* if the only solution to the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}=0\n$$\n\nis ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=0.$ Otherwise, the vectors are *linearly dependent*.\n\nA set containing *only two* vectors is linearly *dependent* if and only if the two vectors are parallel.\n\nFrom the given options, the correct answer is \n\n$$\n{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}-10 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTo see why, notice that \n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}-10 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}=(-2)\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}=-2{a}_{1}.\n$$\n\nThis way, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{a}_{1}-2{a}_{1} & =0 \\\\ 2{a}_{1}+{a}_{2} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn other words, the vectors ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{2}$ are parallel.\n\nTo see why this means that ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{2}$ are linearly dependent, we notice that the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}=0\n$$\n\nhas the solution ${x}_{1}=2$ and ${x}_{2}=1,$ which is different from ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=0.$ Therefore, the set is linearly dependent."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186241031 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "87ecc4be-4578-57d6-a249-a80e721e206a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447718} {:answer/id #uuid "ef287bfc-2ff4-5b14-b2d5-1bc2198e03c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447719}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "87ecc4be-4578-57d6-a249-a80e721e206a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447718} :answer-field/id #uuid "128bee5d-a4a7-57a1-ae6a-7583c0f715e8" :answer-field/key "The equation ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=0$ has only the trivial solution ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448899} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dbe9b5d3-6adb-5955-bcd2-adef03763ddd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447720} {:answer/id #uuid "41f14142-f395-5b2d-97b2-a7334b9547d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447721}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "41f14142-f395-5b2d-97b2-a7334b9547d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447721} :answer-field/id #uuid "e2ed73d9-5758-5bb8-b978-25fc615c46b3" :answer-field/key "The vectors ${a}_{1},{a}_{2},$ and ${a}_{3}$ are linearly dependent." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448900} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "530e368b-e235-51ad-89b6-cae0058759c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447722} {:answer/id #uuid "a1b0c5a9-4103-56d9-a943-e66ba874a356" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447723}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "530e368b-e235-51ad-89b6-cae0058759c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447722} :answer-field/id #uuid "114dd27c-9db0-5c20-a81a-10eeefb53fbc" :answer-field/key "The vectors ${a}_{1},{a}_{2},$ and ${a}_{3}$ are linearly independent." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448901}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "c05cb83d-c779-50b1-a772-7d4551eea239" :question/math-academy-id "q-105308" :question/problem "Consider the following vectors:\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 10 \\\\ -12\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{3}=\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 8 \\\\ -16\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nAssume that ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},$ and ${x}_{3}$ are real numbers. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "We say that three vectors ${v}_{1},{v}_{2},$ and ${v}_{3}$ are *linearly independent* if the only solution to the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}+{x}_{3}{v}_{3}=0\n$$\n\nis ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0.$ Otherwise, the vectors are *linearly dependent*.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\nThe equation ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=0$ corresponds to the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}+4{x}_{3} &=0 \\\\ 3{x}_{1}+10{x}_{2}+8{x}_{3} &=0 \\\\ -4{x}_{1}-12{x}_{2}-16{x}_{3} &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nTo solve the system, we create its augmented matrix and reduce it using Gaussian elimination:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 3 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 10 & 8 & 0 \\\\ -4 & -12 & -16 & 0\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 3 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 & 0 \\\\ -4 & -12 & -16 & 0\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 3 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the matrix above, we conclude that the basic variables are ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$, while ${x}_{3}$ is the free variable. \n\nSince there is one free variable, the equation ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=0$ has an infinite number of nonzero solutions, which means that the vectors are linearly dependent. \n\nTherefore, statements “The equation ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=0$ has only the trivial solution ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0.$” and “The vectors ${a}_{1},{a}_{2},$ and ${a}_{3}$ are linearly independent” are false, while statement “The vectors ${a}_{1},{a}_{2},$ and ${a}_{3}$ are linearly dependent” is true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186241033 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6b0bd8cc-6ac8-5e72-b06f-73c1654ffe1e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461413} {:answer/id #uuid "e80cc002-b38f-5d3e-892e-0841eebc40e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 