f 17592186461417} :answer-field/id #uuid "4f68b655-e005-5eb7-8191-01334bd4f1ec" :answer-field/key "The vectors ${a}_{1},{a}_{2},$ and ${a}_{3}$ are linearly independent." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462462} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "732e0602-3cba-547c-8036-108d2abc2a81" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186667808} {:answer/id #uuid "c08d3ed4-ac72-56ec-b285-734990204a6c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186667809}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "732e0602-3cba-547c-8036-108d2abc2a81" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186667808} :answer-field/id #uuid "ba9a1a20-3f2b-5ae1-8ce3-15b1fe9b26ed" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668181}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "af32236d-520e-5b71-b7ec-9663a181498c" :question/math-academy-id "q-105310" :question/problem "Consider the following vectors:\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ 15 \\\\ -7\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{3}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nAssume that ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},$ and ${x}_{3}$ are real numbers. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "We say that three vectors ${v}_{1},{v}_{2},$ and ${v}_{3}$ are *linearly independent* if the only solution to the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}+{x}_{3}{v}_{3}=0\n$$\n\nis ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0.$ Otherwise, the vectors are *linearly dependent*.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\nThe equation ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=0$ corresponds to the system \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}+7{x}_{2}-{x}_{3} &=0 \\\\ 4{x}_{1}+15{x}_{2}-4{x}_{3} &=0 \\\\ -2{x}_{1}-7{x}_{2}+{x}_{3} &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nTo solve the system, we create its augmented matrix and reduce it using Gaussian elimination:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}2 & 7 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 15 & -4 & 0 \\\\ -2 & -7 & 1 & 0\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}2 & 7 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ -2 & -7 & 1 & 0\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}2 & 7 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the matrix above, we conclude that the basic variables are ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$, while ${x}_{3}$ is the free variable. \n\nSince there is one free variable, the equation ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=0$ has an infinite number of nonzero solutions, which means that the vectors are linearly dependent. \n\nTherefore, statement “The vectors ${a}_{1},{a}_{2},$ and ${a}_{3}$ are linearly independent” is false, while statements “The equation ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=0$  has an infinite number of nonzero solutions” and “The vectors ${a}_{1},{a}_{2},$ and ${a}_{3}$ are linearly dependent” are true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186241036 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cd10af90-8268-5232-9473-253f1c4a0da2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447724} {:answer/id #uuid "f54d7916-c701-5bcb-a279-b7f11eb4abc1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447725}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cd10af90-8268-5232-9473-253f1c4a0da2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db